{
  "//": [
    "Third-party skill sources — someone else's repo of agent skills you want",
    "installed alongside this engine's own workflow skills.",
    "",
    "This file does NOT belong in the engine checkout. Put it beside rules/ in",
    "whatever private content repo this machine points at, and name it in the",
    "machine config:",
    "",
    "    SBW_SKILLS_MANIFEST=~/dev-conventions/skills.json",
    "",
    "The reason is the same one rules/ ships empty here: a public engine that",
    "shipped a curated roster of another person's skills would be shipping an",
    "opinion. The mechanism is the engine's; the roster is yours.",
    "",
    "Then: `make fetch-skills` (preview) / `make fetch-skills YES=1` to clone",
    "each source at its pin, and `make sync-skills` to link them in.",
    "`make doctor` reports a source that is unfetched, sitting at the wrong sha,",
    "or linked without being declared. A '//' key is a comment and is ignored,",
    "so this file is a valid manifest as it stands — copy it and edit in place.",
    "",
    "The all-zero refs below are refused rather than attempted, so a copy you",
    "have not finished editing says so instead of failing later inside git.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  name           required. Becomes the directory under vendor/external/,",
    "                 so it must be a single safe path segment.",
    "  repo           required. Anything `git clone` accepts.",
    "  ref            required, and a full 40-character sha unless you enjoy",
    "                 surprises. An unpinned source means two machines reading",
    "                 this file install different skills on different days.",
    "  allow          required. Per-source allowlist, by skill directory name.",
    "                 There is no 'install everything' — each skill you adopt is",
    "                 charged against the same session budget as your own, and",
    "                 the one roster that was chosen wholesale turned out to want",
    "                 three of six.",
    "  skills_subdir  optional, defaults to 'skills'. Where in that repo the",
    "                 skill directories live. Use '.' for a suite that puts skill",
    "                 directories at its repo root.",
    "  license        optional, free text (an SPDX id, or a sentence about why",
    "                 there isn't one). Omitting it WARNS on every run: what you",
    "                 are allowed to do with someone else's content is asked once",
    "                 at adoption and then never again, so it wants a mechanical",
    "                 prompt. An unlicensed repo is all-rights-reserved by default.",
    "  applies_to     optional path globs. Purely for reporting: `make skills-for",
    "                 REPO=...` and the onboard-repo skill use it to say which",
    "                 skills are scoped to a repo. Omit it and the skill is",
    "                 treated as applying everywhere, which is reported as such",
    "                 rather than as a miss.",
    "",
    "A 'candidates' array records skills you have deliberately NOT adopted, so",
    "onboarding can mention them. This is the one thing the agent host cannot do",
    "for itself: it routes to the skills that are installed and can say nothing",
    "about one that exists and is not. Fields: name, repo and when are required;",
    "install, license, applies_to and status are optional. Keep `when` honest",
    "about the cost, not only the benefit — the reason to read it is to decide.",
    "",
    "  status         suggested (default) | adopted | declined. Only `suggested`",
    "                 is pitched; the other two are decisions already made, and",
    "                 they stay in the list rather than being deleted because the",
    "                 value of a rejected option is the reason it was rejected.",
    "                 Delete it and the next session re-evaluates from scratch.",
    "                 `adopted` covers a skill installed the vendor's own way,",
    "                 which is genuinely adopted while appearing in no allow list.",
    "",
    "Any key starting with '//' is a comment, at every level, so each section can",
    "carry its own note. A typo still fails, because a typo does not start with //.",
    "",
    "A skill of your own with the same name always wins — sync reports the",
    "shadowing rather than silently preferring one."
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "name": "example-motion",
      "repo": "https://github.com/example/motion-skills",
      "ref": "0000000000000000000000000000000000000000",
      "license": "MIT",
      "allow": ["animate", "review-animations"]
    },
    {
      "name": "example-store-assets",
      "repo": "https://github.com/example/store-screenshots",
      "ref": "0000000000000000000000000000000000000000",
      "skills_subdir": "skills",
      "license": "MIT",
      "applies_to": ["app.json", "app.config.*", "eas.json"],
      "allow": ["app-store-screenshots"]
    }
  ],
  "//candidates": [
    "Not installed. Reported by `make skills-for REPO=...` and by onboard-repo,",
    "which name them and never install them: adopting a skill is a standing choice",
    "about every future session, and some write into the project."
  ],
  "candidates": [
    {
      "name": "example-design-linter",
      "repo": "https://github.com/example/design-linter",
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "when": "design-heavy frontend wanting a visual-polish pass. Invasive: writes files at the project root and registers an edit-time hook. Project scope only, never global.",
      "install": "npx example-design-linter install --scope=project",
      "applies_to": ["**/*.tsx", "**/*.css"]
    }
  ]
}
